\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {V}{\ignorespaces Comparison of how different frameworks address selected quantities. ``Predicted'' indicates a zero-parameter numerical prediction with stated accuracy. ``Consistent'' means the topology produces the result but the derivation uses standard physics (Gauss's law in $d = 3$). ``Geometric'' indicates a novel structural argument (the face ratio). ``Reinterpreted'' means the result is algebraically equivalent to the definition but given a new physical interpretation. Each framework has different goals; the comparison reflects scope, not quality.}}{46}{table.5}\protected@file@percent }
